<title>
APP Sensor On-Vehicle Inspection
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check that accelerator pedal assembly (incorporating APP sensor) is mounted to vehicle body properly (no pinched floor carpet, etc.).
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If mounting is improper, reinstall accelerator pedal assembly. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1316007"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Connect SUZUKI scan tool to DLC with ignition “OFF”.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Set ignition “ON” and select “Data List” mode.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1 page = "2">
<ptxt>
Check that voltage varies depending on accelerator pedal position as shown in the following graph.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If faulty condition is found, check the following points.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Wire harness and connections
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
APP sensor: 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1316008"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
